 in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Talking About Future Actions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use two different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.</li><li>When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">going to</span>.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Structure</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll start with you.</span> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Will you start with me?</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">We won't be starting with you. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'm going to write a feature on friendship for the magazine.</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Are you going to write a feature for the magazine?</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm not going to write a feature for it.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Used to and Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> and  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> have rather similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "However, there is an important difference between  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and  <span class=\"strong\">would</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the following example: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We used to visit India.</span> (correct)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "However, when <span class=\"strong\">would</span> replaces <span class=\"strong\">used</span>, the same example becomes ungrammatical:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We would visit India.</span> (not correct)<br> <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer when we were children.</span> (correct)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We used to organize our own sports competitions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We would give prizes to everyone.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "feature", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a long article in a magazine about one particular subject", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm writing a feature on childhood memories.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about childhood friends.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "friendship", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the state of being friends", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm writing a feature on childhood friendships.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "buddy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "friend", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My dad used to take me and my buddies to watch baseball games.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ice skating ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a form of physical activity performed on an icy surface with special boots", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We used to go ice skating.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rink", "type": "name"}, {"content": " an enclosed icy surface where people can practice ice skating", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't have time to get on the rink now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "freezie", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sweet frozen treat; popsicle", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love freezies in the summer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pop", "type": "name"}, {"content": "soda", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cola is my favorite kind of pop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a text (10-14 lines) about your childhood.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe what you used to do all the time. Remember to write about your habits in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe the friends you had as a kid.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your text aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about habits in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about friendships and relationships.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe actions in the past.", "type": "text"}]}]}